Hi everybody,

I am a bit confused with the H function (total entropy). According to what I have understood, more the value of H is close to 1, more the level of biodiversity of the place studied is high, more H is close to 0, less there is biodversity.
I did a test with too recordings that I have registered in the same place and at the same date: we can clearly hear the song a bird on the first one, and nothing (just the background noise) on the second one. However, the H value of the first is inferior to the second, it's not logical for me... Do I misanderstood this index? Someone have an idea of why I obtain this?

